{
	"version": 1,
	"_comment": "Which sound plays for what. client/audio/audio_director.gd (autoload Audio) reads this; adding or changing a sound is an edit here, not code. cues: name -> files (one is picked at random, not the same twice in a row), bus, volume_db, pitch [min,max], volume_jitter_db, max_voices (copies of this cue at once; the oldest is cut), cooldown_ms (re-triggers sooner are ignored), priority (1-10: lowest loses its voice when the pool is full), positional (false = not quieter with distance), duck_music_db + duck_seconds (stingers dip the music). events: simulation event type -> rules checked in order; a rule plays its cues when every 'when' fact matches (a value, a list of allowed values, or {min,max}); 'stop' ends the list; pitch_from raises the pitch with a numeric fact. {weapon} in a cue name becomes the fighter's move set. Facts are made in client/audio/audio_rules.gd facts(). ui: action -> cue for Audio.play_ui(). auto_ui: what every Button / TabBar plays by itself (a node can set meta audio_ui to another ui action, or to an empty string for silence). music / ambience: id -> looping file. scenes: scene file -> music + ambience (ambience_by_map uses GameState.selected_map_id).",
